# XSH kill_dependency()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.

assertion  XSH.kill_dependency.001
anchor     functions/kill_dependency.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/stdatomic.h.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       <stdatomic.h> defines the macro kill_dependency, and
           kill_dependency(y) is the value of y for int, long, unsigned long
           long, double, _Bool, char, an expression, and object, structure
           and function pointers.
test       t/001-value.c

assertion  XSH.kill_dependency.002
anchor     functions/kill_dependency.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/kill_dependency.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2024
says       A pointer published with atomic_store_explicit(release) and read by
           another thread with atomic_load_explicit(consume) points to
           the published data: kill_dependency() of a member read through it
           is the data written before publication (2000 messages).
note       The wait is bounded (20 s); not seeing a message is UNRESOLVED.
test       t/002-consume-chain.c
